menu "Attadipa firmware"

config ATTADIPA_WATCH_CONTROL
    bool "USB watch-control endpoint"
    default n
    help
        Enable the debug control plane over USB-Serial/JTAG: screenshots,
        remote input, and the time and mesh provisioning opcodes. Any host
        that can open the port can use all of it; there is no
        authentication, so this is a bench image rather than a product one.
        Physical touch and the case buttons are NOT gated by this symbol --
        they live in physical_input.cpp and are in every image (#346).
        The feature owns one full RGB565 frame in PSRAM while running.

config ATTADIPA_I2C_PROBE
    bool "I2C bring-up probe"
    default n
    help
        Scan the I2C bus on the pins below and log every address that
        acknowledges, then read the AXP2101 charge-voltage register if one
        answered. A bring-up instrument for a board this firmware has no
        driver for; it writes no register and asserts no board identity.

config ATTADIPA_I2C_PROBE_SDA
    int "I2C probe SDA GPIO"
    depends on ATTADIPA_I2C_PROBE
    default 10

config ATTADIPA_I2C_PROBE_SCL
    int "I2C probe SCL GPIO"
    depends on ATTADIPA_I2C_PROBE
    default 11

endmenu
